A private school in Bamenda is equipping its office computers. The principal lists these needs:

- type letters and report cards;
- keep pupils' records so that any pupil can be found by name or class;
- calculate the term averages;
- run all of these programs on the computers;
- keep the computers free of malicious programs.

For each need, name the category of software that meets it. Then explain why the school cannot use the other programs without one particular piece of system software.
